[h1]Welcome to the Official Project Vigilance Collection[/h1]
[b]Targeting RimWorld 1.7 (Waylith Engine)[/b]

[b]Project Vigilance[/b] is a modular systems overhaul bringing the strategic depth, planetary paranoia, and technological escalation of classic X-COM to RimWorld.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Design Philosophy[/h2]

[list]
[*] [b]Standalone Frameworks:[/b] Each core system (overland marching, sensory grids, ground interception, or containment) has zero alien or sci-fi prerequisites. You can drop them into vanilla, medieval, industrial, or spacer playthroughs.
[*] [b]The Full Overhaul:[/b] When combined, the modules form an authentic planetary defence campaign complete with global surveillance, interception scrambles, panic management, and extraterrestrial threat progression.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Modules in this Collection[/h2]

[list]
[*] [b]Project Vigilance - Overland Incursions [v0.3.0 LIVE]:[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Replaces instantaneous map-edge teleportation with physical, real-time planetary transit across the globe for raids, trade caravans, and visitors.
    [*] [b]Ground Interception & Tactical Ambush:[/b] Intercept approaching forces on the global hex grid before they reach the colony. Launch stalking ambushes or surprise sleeping warbands in night raids.
    [*] [b]Retreat Lifecycle & Kidnap Rescue:[/b] Fleeing enemies physically retreat with 1:1 wounds, carried loot, and captive colonists. Intercept them on the road or assault their stronghold to liberate incarcerated prisoners.
    [*] [b]Evacuated Colony Hierarchy:[/b] Raiders reaching vacant colonies execute 3-tier tactical decision-making—scouring for tracks to pursue fleeing caravans, retargeting secondary outposts, or ransack and march home.
    [*] [b]Night Owl & Schedule-Aware Caravaning:[/b] Timetable-aware travel allows Night Owls to sleep daytime (11:00–18:00) and march through the night, while mixed squads maintain 24/7 camp watch.
    [*] [b]Classic 3-Tier Haze of War:[/b] Shrouded (unexplored mask), Obscured (surveyed terrain), and Monitored (live sensory visibility).
    [*] [b]Sensory Horizons & Watertight Security:[/b] Colony and caravan lookouts project realistic sight lines that dynamically reduce by 50% during darkness; all undetected contacts receive persistent tracking numbers ([i]Contact-1[/i], [i]Contact-2[/i]).
    [*] [b]Pack Animal Cargo & Roadside Trading:[/b] Trade stock is carried in pack animal inventories across all battle maps; barter with merchants on the road.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Harmony:[/b] Core dependency required for engine assembly patching.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Upcoming Modules (Roadmap)[/h2]

[list]
[*] [b]Module 1: Advanced Radar Infrastructure & Early Warning [Next Up]:[/b] Tech-tree early-warning radar domes, listening posts, sensory towers, and oceanic sonar grids.
[*] [b]Inter-Faction Encounters & Trade Routes:[/b] Persistent NPC-to-NPC trade routes, cross-faction skirmishes, and grounded storyteller road meetings.
[*] [b]Module 2: Interception & Rapid Response:[/b] Long-range craft scrambles, aerial dogfights, drop-pod rapid response, and tactical crash site recoveries.
[*] [b]Module 3: Alien Containment & Biology:[/b] Stasis cells, live prisoner interrogations, autopsies, and the "Fog of Research".
[*] [b]Module 4: Invasion Campaign & Planetary Panic:[/b] Planetary Council funding, regional panic meters, and Alien Doom Clock progression.
[*] [b]Aquatic Operations (TftD Layer):[/b] Submersibles, coastal sonar arrays, and seabed salvage operations.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

